{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdgeLemmas","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdgeLemmas","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Intervals","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.antisymm_double_sum_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.antisymm_double_sum_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":449,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L449-L458","doc":"The finite half of the lattice cancellation: an antisymmetric kernel summed over `H × H`\nvanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.tail_move_lt_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.tail_move_lt_zero","kind":"theorem","line":436,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L436-L447","doc":"The strict form: a move touching the tail rows `H ≠ ∅` loses, given a negative bracket and a\nnon-improving lower part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.tail_never_helps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.tail_never_helps","kind":"theorem","line":419,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L419-L434","doc":"**Tail lemma (M7), structural form.**  Split a move `S = L ∪ H` (disjoint, inside the block).\nIf every row of `H` contributes at most `β` (the per-row bracket — the hypothesis that carries\nthe lattice-cancellation estimate), then `gain(S) ≤ gain(L) + |H|·β`; with `β < 0`,\n`gain(L) ≤ 0` and `H ≠ ∅` the move strictly loses, so the rows of `H` never help. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.moveBy_union","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.moveBy_union","kind":"theorem","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L409-L417","doc":"`v + χ_{L ∪ H} = (v + χ_L) + χ_H` for disjoint `L`, `H`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.pairObjective_move_gain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.pairObjective_move_gain","kind":"theorem","line":342,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L342-L407","doc":"**Move-gain decomposition.**  For any two-body objective and `H ⊆ range n`, the gain of the\nmove `+χ_H` is `Σ_{j∈H}` (one-body change of `j` + change of each pair with exactly one end, `j`,\nin `H`).  Pairs with both ends in `H` keep their difference and contribute nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.pair_sum_square","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.pair_sum_square","kind":"theorem","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L331-L340","doc":"Pair sum over `i < j < n` written as a full square sum, for swapping. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.rowGain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.rowGain","kind":"def","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L325-L329","doc":"What row `j ∈ H` contributes to a `+χ_H` move: its one-body change plus the change of every\npair whose other end is outside `H`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.crossChange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.crossChange","kind":"def","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L319-L323","doc":"The change of the pair `{j, x}` when `j` alone moves up by one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.moveBy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.moveBy","kind":"def","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L316-L317","doc":"The point `v + χ_H`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.wall_persists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.wall_persists","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L301-L306","doc":"The wall condition persists: with `a > 0`, `ε(1) < a·P₀` gives `ε(1) < a·P` for all\n`P ≥ P₀`, so the frames beyond the first one meeting it all reduce to it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.frame_succ_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.frame_succ_le","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L278-L299","doc":"**Frame `pe + 1` adds nothing (M8 + M9).**  When `ε(1) < a·(pe + 1)`, every value of the\n`(pe + 1)`-frame objective at a domain point is at most a value of the `pe`-frame objective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.frameObjective_bottom_raise_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.frameObjective_bottom_raise_lt","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L218-L276","doc":"**Wall inequality (M9).**  On frame `P` with `n + 1` rows, at any point of the domain (every\n`ε` and `W` argument touched by the bottom row positive), raising the bottom row by `x ≥ 1`\nstrictly lowers `G`, provided `ε` and `W_m` are antitone on the positive integers, `0 ≤ c`, and\n`ε(1) < a·P`.  The one-body gain is at most `x·ε(1)`, the wall costs `a·P·x`, the tail and the\nquadratic only cost, and the bottom row's pairs only close. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.sum_eps_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.sum_eps_le","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L205-L216","doc":"`Σ_{k<x} ε(1 + k) ≤ x·ε(1)` for `ε` antitone on the positive integers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.frameObjective_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.frameObjective_shift","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L181-L203","doc":"**Shift identity (M8):** `G_{pe+1}(0, u) = G_pe(u)`, for every `ε`, `W`, `a`, `c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.telescope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.telescope","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L169-L179","doc":"The telescoping behind the shift: a pair that closes from `ε(c) − ε(c + x)` plus the\none-body sum starting one step higher is the one-body sum starting at `c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.frameObjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.frameObjective","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L165-L167","doc":"The bottom-edge objective of frame `pe` on an `n`-row block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.framePsi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.framePsi","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L161-L163","doc":"The pair piece of rows `i < j`: `ε(g_{ij}) − ε(g_{ij} + d)`, `g_{ij} = b_j − b_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.framePhi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.framePhi","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L152-L159","doc":"The one-body piece of row `j` at displacement `x`:\n`Σ_{k<x} ε(b_j + 1 + k)` (`= R(b_j) − R(b_j + x)`) `+ W_m(h_j) − W_m(h_j − x) − a·w_j·x − c·x²`,\nwith `m = pe − n` and `h_j = b_n − b_j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.wallWeight_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.wallWeight_zero","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L149-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.wallWeight_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.wallWeight_succ","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L146-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.rowBase_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.rowBase_zero","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L143-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.rowBase_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.rowBase_succ","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L140-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.wallWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.wallWeight","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L137-L138","doc":"The wall's linear weight `w_j = pe − j` (zero above the wall). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.rowBase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.rowBase","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L134-L135","doc":"`b_j` in frame `pe`: `j` on the wall (`j < pe`), `2j − pe` on the gap-2 lattice above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.pairObjective_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.pairObjective_shift","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L107-L124","doc":"**Shift identity, abstract form.**  If the rows `j ≥ 1` of `(φ', ψ')` are the rows `j − 1`\nof `(φ, ψ)` — except that row `j + 1`'s one-body piece plus its pair with an undisplaced bottom\nrow equals `φ j` — and the bottom row's one-body piece vanishes at `0`, then\n`G'(0, u) = G(u)`.  Pure reindexing of the two finite sums. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.bottomZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.bottomZero","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L102-L105","doc":"The block with an undisplaced bottom row prepended: `(0, u)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.pairObjective_succ_bottom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.pairObjective_succ_bottom","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L86-L100","doc":"Peel the bottom row off a two-body objective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.pairObjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.XbotBottomEdge.pairObjective","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/XbotBottomEdgeLemmas.lean#L82-L84","doc":"`G(u) = Σ_{j<n} φ_j(u_j) + Σ_{i<j<n} ψ_{ij}(u_j − u_i)` over integer displacements `u ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}